//! ASHRAE 140-2023 §9b comparative execution harness — Issue #4666.
//!
//! # What this module does
//!
//! `data/reference/ashrae140/section9b_ce_comparative_cases.json` (the §9b
//! comparative case table, generated by `scripts/generate_section9b_cases.py`)
//! pairs every CE100–CE200 case with its transcribed IEA SHC Task-22
//! comparative evidence range — or, for the five cases the bounds file does
//! not cover, with an explicit missing-band note. The table itself carries no
//! engine value and no verdict: it is evidence, not a criterion.
//!
//! This module closes the loop for the §9b view of the family:
//!
//! 1. **Every** CE case (CE100–CE200, 14 of them) is executed through the
//!    existing §9 equipment dispatch — the same path the §9a engine-run
//!    harness uses (`fluxion::sim::hvac::CePerformanceMap` via
//!    `dispatch_ce_steady_state`) — deterministically, with no weather file
//!    and no synthetic data.
//! 2. Each case's engine values are scored against **that case's own §9b
//!    bands**, read verbatim from the §9b table (`bands[].band_low_si` /
//!    `band_high_si` plus the recorded-unit edges). Every scored row records
//!    the band kind, the band source and the band's provenance.
//! 3. Rows that fall outside their band are **recorded as known-fail rows
//!    with the real numbers** (engine value, band edges, gap) in
//!    `data/section9b_engine_run_results.json`, which this module verifies
//!    against the live engine run on every test execution.
//! 4. The five unbanded cases (CE165, CE180, CE185, CE190, CE195) carry
//!    their explicit missing-band notes — verbatim from the §9b table — and
//!    **no** band, **no** engine verdict and **no** invented range.
//!
//! Nothing here fits a band to the engine output and nothing widens a band:
//! the bands are read verbatim from the committed §9b artefact.
//!
//! # Scope limits (hard stops, honoured here)
//!
//! * The ASHRAE 140-2023 §9.3 comparative test series is **not** implemented
//!   in this tree and is **not** implemented here: this harness executes the
//!   CE cases through the engine's §9 equipment dispatch and scores the
//!   resulting steady-state values against the committed evidence ranges. It
//!   runs no comparative-series protocol, derives no series verdict, and does
//!   not close the §9.3 coverage gap.
//! * Every band keeps its committed label — "comparative evidence range, not
//!   a pass/fail criterion" — on every row. A `pass` / `known_fail` status
//!   therefore means "inside / outside the evidence range", never "the case
//!   passes / fails the standard".
//! * No band is transcribed for the five unbanded cases: CE165, CE180,
//!   CE185, CE190 and CE195 stay explicitly unbanded.
//!
//! # Which dispatch runs the cases, and why not the coil/fan chain
//!
//! The §9 CE family is *unitary space-cooling equipment*: in this tree its
//! engine representation is the DX performance map (`CePerformanceMap`,
//! Tables 9-5…9-10 of 140-2023) together with the steady-state dispatch in
//! `section9_ce.rs`. The generic `CoolingCoil` / `FanComponent` /
//! pressure-air-loop component chain models water/duct-side equipment with a
//! transcribed air-side state; the §9 unitary DX cases have no transcribed
//! air flow, duct topology or coil leaving-air state (the §9 input
//! specification is licensed, Issue #4285), so routing them through that
//! chain would mean inventing inputs. The harness therefore uses the
//! equipment dispatch that *is* committed for §9 — the same one the §9a
//! harness uses — and records the same quantities.
//!
//! # The entering wet-bulb
//!
//! The map is tabulated over (ODB × EWB) with EDB columns. A CE case fixes
//! its ODB (and its setpoint = EDB), but **its own EWB is not transcribed**
//! for 13 of the 14 cases; the single exception is CE200, whose condition
//! *is* the map's own AHRI rating point (EWB 19.4 °C). As in the §9a
//! harness, each case is dispatched at **every entering wet-bulb column the
//! map itself tabulates** (15.0 / 17.2 / 19.4 / 21.7 °C, read from the
//! committed map artefact, not hard-coded) and the resulting envelope is
//! reported. No column is attributed to a case.
//!
//! # Band metrics and why most of them cannot be scored
//!
//! The §9b bands carry up to three metrics per case: `annual_cooling`
//! (MWh), `peak_cooling` (kW) and — for CE150 — `max_zone_temp` (°C).
//!
//! * `annual_cooling` is an **annual** quantity: it needs the normative TMY2
//!   weather file the standard binds the case to (`CE100A`, `CE110A`,
//!   `CE165A`, `CE200A`) — licensed supplemental material that is never
//!   committed to this repository. A steady-state equipment dispatch has no
//!   duty cycle, so this metric is recorded as **not reproducible**, with the
//!   band edges shown.
//! * `max_zone_temp` is a zone-temperature trajectory output of an annual
//!   run; a steady-state dispatch holds the case setpoint by construction.
//!   Also **not reproducible**.
//! * `peak_cooling` (kW) is the only band metric a steady-state equipment
//!   dispatch can produce. It is scored against the engine's **full-load
//!   cooling power at the case condition** (compressor power + the map's
//!   230 W indoor fan heat, adjusted-net basis) — the same definition the
//!   §9a harness uses. The ensemble's own metric semantics (peak cooling
//!   *load* vs peak cooling *power*) are **not verifiable from this tree**
//!   (the bounds CSV records `source_page` as `pending`), so every scored
//!   row carries that caveat, and the engine's required cooling load (the
//!   alternative reading) is recorded alongside.
//!
//! # Status vocabulary
//!
//! * `pass` — the engine value falls inside the comparative evidence range.
//! * `known_fail` — the engine value falls outside it; recorded with the real
//!   numbers, never omitted.
//! * `not_reproducible` — the band metric cannot be produced by this run.
//! * `no_band` — no band exists for that metric/case (the five unbanded
//!   cases, and the metrics the bounds file does not cover).
//!
//! # Re-recording the results file
//!
//! ```text
//! FLUXION_SECTION9B_WRITE_RESULTS=tests/validation/hvac_equipment_rated_performance/data/section9b_engine_run_results.json \
//!   cargo test --test hvac_equipment_rated_performance section9b_
//! ```
//!
//! The re-record path is explicit and opt-in; the ordinary test run always
//! compares the live engine run against the committed file.

use std::collections::BTreeMap;

use serde_json::{json, Map, Value};

use fluxion::sim::hvac::{CePerformanceMap, CeTable};

use super::section9_ce::dispatch_ce_steady_state;

/// The §9b comparative case table (generated by `scripts/generate_section9b_cases.py`).
const SECTION9B_CASES_JSON: &str = include_str!(concat!(
    env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR"),
    "/data/reference/ashrae140/section9b_ce_comparative_cases.json"
));
/// The §9a case definitions (conditions, weather binding) — the engine input.
const SECTION9_CASES_JSON: &str = include_str!(concat!(
    env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR"),
    "/data/reference/ashrae140/section9_ce_cases.json"
));
/// The CE100 performance map (Tables 9-5…9-10 of 140-2023).
const SECTION9_MAP_JSON: &str = include_str!(concat!(
    env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR"),
    "/data/reference/ashrae140/section9_ce100_performance_map.json"
));
/// The recorded per-case §9b rows (the known-fail record).
const SECTION9B_RESULTS_JSON: &str = include_str!("data/section9b_engine_run_results.json");

/// Opt-in path for re-recording the results file (see the module docs).
const WRITE_RESULTS_ENV: &str = "FLUXION_SECTION9B_WRITE_RESULTS";

/// The exact band-kind label the §9b table uses. Standard 140 defines no
/// pass/fail criterion for the Task-22 comparative ranges; every scored row
/// carries this label verbatim.
const BAND_KIND: &str = "comparative evidence range, not a pass/fail criterion";

/// Relative tolerance for the live-vs-recorded comparison (the recorded file
/// stores values rounded to 1e-6).
const RECORDED_RTOL: f64 = 1e-6;
/// Absolute tolerance for the live-vs-recorded comparison.
const RECORDED_ATOL: f64 = 1e-9;

/// The five cases the Task-22 bounds file does not cover.
const UNBANDED_CASES: [&str; 5] = ["CE165", "CE180", "CE185", "CE190", "CE195"];

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Committed artefacts
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn load_section9b_cases() -> Vec<Value> {
    let root: Value =
        serde_json::from_str(SECTION9B_CASES_JSON).expect("parse §9b comparative case table");
    root["cases"].as_array().expect("cases array").clone()
}

fn load_section9_cases() -> Vec<Value> {
    let root: Value = serde_json::from_str(SECTION9_CASES_JSON).expect("parse §9 CE cases");
    root["cases"].as_array().expect("cases array").clone()
}

fn load_map() -> CePerformanceMap {
    CePerformanceMap::from_json_str(SECTION9_MAP_JSON).expect("parse §9 CE100 performance map")
}

fn map_json() -> Value {
    serde_json::from_str(SECTION9_MAP_JSON).expect("parse §9 CE100 performance map json")
}

/// The map's own tabulated entering wet-bulb columns (°C), read from the
/// committed map artefact rather than restated in code.
fn map_ewb_columns() -> Vec<f64> {
    let root = map_json();
    let table = &root["tables"]["adjusted_net_Table_26e"];
    let row = table
        .as_object()
        .expect("adjusted-net table object")
        .values()
        .next()
        .expect("adjusted-net table has an ODB row");
    let mut cols: Vec<f64> = row
        .as_object()
        .expect("EWB row object")
        .keys()
        .filter_map(|k| k.parse::<f64>().ok())
        .collect();
    cols.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).expect("finite EWB"));
    assert!(!cols.is_empty(), "map exposes no EWB column");
    cols
}

/// Indoor fan heat (W) on the adjusted-net basis, from the map artefact.
fn fan_heat_w() -> f64 {
    map_json()["fan_heat"]["actual_W"]
        .as_f64()
        .expect("fan_heat.actual_W")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// One engine dispatch
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// One §9 CE case dispatched at one tabulated entering wet-bulb.
#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
struct CaseRun {
    entering_wet_bulb_c: f64,
    outdoor_dry_bulb_c: f64,
    entering_dry_bulb_c: f64,
    /// Full-load total (sensible + latent) capacity at the condition [W].
    total_capacity_w: f64,
    /// Full-load sensible capacity at the condition [W].
    sensible_capacity_w: f64,
    /// Full-load compressor power at the condition [W].
    compressor_power_w: f64,
    /// Full-load cooling power (compressor + indoor fan) [kW] — the quantity
    /// scored against the `peak_cooling` band.
    peak_cooling_power_kw: f64,
    /// The case's required cooling load (sensible + latent gains) [W].
    required_load_w: f64,
    /// The case's required load [kW] — the alternative reading of the
    /// `peak_cooling` band metric, recorded for transparency.
    required_load_kw: f64,
    /// Part-load ratio from the load balance (clamped to [0, 1]).
    plr: f64,
    /// Delivered capacity at the operating point [W].
    delivered_capacity_w: f64,
    /// Delivered compressor power at the operating point [W].
    delivered_power_w: f64,
    /// Shortfall of the delivered load against the required load [W].
    capacity_shortfall_w: f64,
    /// Sensible heat ratio at the operating point.
    shr: f64,
    /// COP at the operating point (total capacity / (compressor + fan)).
    cop: f64,
}

/// Dispatch one CE case at one entering wet-bulb through the engine's DX
/// performance map (the same path `dispatch_ce_steady_state` uses).
fn run_case(case: &Value, map: &CePerformanceMap, ewb_c: f64, fan_w: f64) -> CaseRun {
    let cond = &case["conditions"];
    let odb_c = cond["outdoor_dry_bulb_C"].as_f64().expect("ODB");
    let edb_c = cond["cooling_setpoint_C"].as_f64().expect("setpoint");
    let full = map.evaluate(CeTable::AdjustedNet26e, ewb_c, odb_c, edb_c, 1.0, fan_w);
    let dispatch = dispatch_ce_steady_state(case, map, ewb_c, fan_w);
    CaseRun {
        entering_wet_bulb_c: ewb_c,
        outdoor_dry_bulb_c: odb_c,
        entering_dry_bulb_c: edb_c,
        total_capacity_w: full.total_capacity_w,
        sensible_capacity_w: full.sensible_capacity_w,
        compressor_power_w: full.compressor_power_w,
        peak_cooling_power_kw: (full.compressor_power_w + fan_w) / 1000.0,
        required_load_w: dispatch.required_load_w,
        required_load_kw: dispatch.required_load_w / 1000.0,
        plr: dispatch.plr,
        delivered_capacity_w: dispatch.delivered_capacity_w,
        delivered_power_w: dispatch.delivered_power_w,
        capacity_shortfall_w: (dispatch.required_load_w - dispatch.delivered_capacity_w).max(0.0),
        shr: dispatch.shr,
        cop: dispatch.cop,
    }
}

/// Round to 1e-6 so the recorded file stays readable and stable.
fn round6(x: f64) -> f64 {
    if !x.is_finite() {
        return x;
    }
    (x * 1e6).round() / 1e6
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Band scoring
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Gap as a percentage of the band midpoint — the repository's strict-gate
/// convention: 0 inside the band, otherwise the distance outside it as a
/// percentage of the midpoint.
fn gap_pct_of_mid(value: f64, low: f64, high: f64) -> f64 {
    let mid = 0.5 * (low + high);
    if value < low {
        if mid <= 0.0 {
            f64::INFINITY
        } else {
            (low - value) / mid * 100.0
        }
    } else if value > high {
        if mid <= 0.0 {
            f64::INFINITY
        } else {
            (value - high) / mid * 100.0
        }
    } else {
        0.0
    }
}

fn direction(value: f64, low: f64, high: f64) -> &'static str {
    if value < low {
        "below"
    } else if value > high {
        "above"
    } else {
        "inside"
    }
}

/// Reason recorded on every `not_reproducible` row: the band metric is an
/// output of the annual case run, which needs the normative weather file.
fn not_reproducible_reason(metric: &str, case_id: &str, weather_file: &str) -> String {
    match metric {
        "annual_cooling" => format!(
            "annual total: the case's normative TMY2 weather file ({weather_file}) is licensed \
             ASHRAE supplemental material and is never committed to this repository \
             (fluxion-core/src/weather/tm2.rs); a steady-state equipment dispatch has no duty \
             cycle, so the annual band cannot be reproduced from the engine run. Tracked as a \
             coverage gap for {case_id} (licensed gate #4285)."
        ),
        "max_zone_temp" | "min_zone_temp" => format!(
            "zone-temperature trajectory output of the annual case run; the steady-state dispatch \
             holds the case setpoint by construction, so no trajectory exists to compare. \
             Tracked as a coverage gap for {case_id} (licensed gate #4285)."
        ),
        other => format!(
            "band metric '{other}' is not produced by the steady-state equipment dispatch \
             (case {case_id}); it is an output of the annual case run and needs the normative \
             weather file (licensed gate #4285)."
        ),
    }
}

/// Build the scored band rows for one case from its committed §9b `bands`.
/// Returns one row per committed band, so no band is silently dropped.
fn band_rows(case: &Value, runs: &[CaseRun], weather_file: &str) -> Vec<Value> {
    let case_id = case["case_id"].as_str().expect("case_id").to_string();
    let weather_file = weather_file.to_string();
    let mut rows: Vec<Value> = Vec::new();

    let bands = case["bands"].as_array().expect("bands array");
    for band in bands {
        let metric = band["metric"].as_str().expect("metric").to_string();
        let kind = band["band_kind"].as_str().expect("band_kind").to_string();
        let source = band["band_source"]
            .as_str()
            .expect("band_source")
            .to_string();
        let low = band["recorded_low"].as_f64().expect("recorded_low");
        let high = band["recorded_high"].as_f64().expect("recorded_high");
        let unit = band["recorded_unit"]
            .as_str()
            .expect("recorded_unit")
            .to_string();
        let low_si = band["band_low_si"].as_f64().expect("band_low_si");
        let high_si = band["band_high_si"].as_f64().expect("band_high_si");
        let unit_si = band["unit_si"].as_str().expect("unit_si").to_string();
        let provenance = band["provenance"].clone();

        let mut row = Map::new();
        row.insert("metric".into(), json!(metric));
        row.insert("band_kind".into(), json!(kind));
        row.insert("band_source".into(), json!(source));
        row.insert("provenance".into(), provenance);
        row.insert("band_low".into(), json!(round6(low)));
        row.insert("band_high".into(), json!(round6(high)));
        row.insert("band_unit".into(), json!(unit));
        row.insert("band_low_si".into(), json!(low_si));
        row.insert("band_high_si".into(), json!(high_si));
        row.insert("band_unit_si".into(), json!(unit_si));

        if metric == "peak_cooling" && unit == "kW" {
            // The only band metric a steady-state equipment dispatch can
            // produce: compare the engine's full-load cooling power at the
            // case condition against the ensemble evidence range.
            let mut inside: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();
            let mut outside: Vec<f64> = Vec::new();
            let mut worst: Option<&CaseRun> = None;
            let mut worst_gap = -1.0_f64;
            for run in runs {
                let gap = gap_pct_of_mid(run.peak_cooling_power_kw, low, high);
                if gap == 0.0 {
                    inside.push(run.entering_wet_bulb_c);
                } else {
                    outside.push(run.entering_wet_bulb_c);
                }
                if gap > worst_gap {
                    worst_gap = gap;
                    worst = Some(run);
                }
            }
            let worst = worst.expect("at least one entering condition");
            let values: Vec<f64> = runs.iter().map(|r| r.peak_cooling_power_kw).collect();
            let min = values.iter().copied().fold(f64::INFINITY, f64::min);
            let max = values.iter().copied().fold(f64::NEG_INFINITY, f64::max);
            let status = if outside.is_empty() {
                "pass"
            } else {
                "known_fail"
            };
            row.insert("engine_metric".into(), json!("peak_cooling_power"));
            row.insert(
                "engine_metric_definition".into(),
                json!(
                    "full-load cooling power at the case condition = compressor power at \
                     PLR=1 + the map's 230 W indoor fan heat (adjusted-net basis)"
                ),
            );
            row.insert(
                "engine_value".into(),
                json!(round6(worst.peak_cooling_power_kw)),
            );
            row.insert("engine_value_unit".into(), json!("kW"));
            row.insert(
                "engine_value_range".into(),
                json!([round6(min), round6(max)]),
            );
            row.insert(
                "engine_required_load_kw".into(),
                json!(round6(worst.required_load_kw)),
            );
            row.insert("gap_pct_of_mid".into(), json!(round6(worst_gap)));
            row.insert(
                "direction".into(),
                json!(direction(worst.peak_cooling_power_kw, low, high)),
            );
            row.insert("inside_at_ewb_C".into(), json!(inside));
            row.insert("outside_at_ewb_C".into(), json!(outside));
            row.insert("status".into(), json!(status));
            row.insert(
                "reason".into(),
                json!(
                    "comparative evidence range scored against the steady-state engine run. The \
                     ensemble metric semantics (peak cooling load vs peak cooling power) are not \
                     verifiable from this tree — the bounds CSV records source_page 'pending' — \
                     so 'pass'/'known_fail' here means inside/outside the evidence range, never \
                     a pass/fail verdict against the standard. The band was read verbatim and \
                     not widened; the case's own entering wet-bulb is untranscribed, so the row \
                     covers every entering condition the map tabulates."
                ),
            );
        } else {
            row.insert("engine_metric".into(), json!(Value::Null));
            row.insert("engine_value".into(), json!(Value::Null));
            row.insert("engine_value_unit".into(), json!(Value::Null));
            row.insert("engine_value_range".into(), json!(Value::Null));
            row.insert("engine_required_load_kw".into(), json!(Value::Null));
            row.insert("gap_pct_of_mid".into(), json!(Value::Null));
            row.insert("direction".into(), json!("not_reproducible"));
            row.insert("inside_at_ewb_C".into(), json!([]));
            row.insert("outside_at_ewb_C".into(), json!([]));
            row.insert("status".into(), json!("not_reproducible"));
            row.insert(
                "reason".into(),
                json!(not_reproducible_reason(&metric, &case_id, &weather_file)),
            );
        }
        rows.push(Value::Object(row));
    }
    rows
}

/// The explicit missing-band notes of a §9b case row (verbatim from the table).
fn missing_band_notes(case: &Value) -> Vec<Value> {
    case["missing_metric_notes"]
        .as_array()
        .expect("missing_metric_notes array")
        .iter()
        .map(|note| {
            let mut row = Map::new();
            row.insert("metric".into(), json!(note["metric"].clone()));
            row.insert("band_kind".into(), json!(Value::Null));
            row.insert("status".into(), json!("no_band"));
            row.insert("note".into(), json!(note["comparative_note"].clone()));
            Value::Object(row)
        })
        .collect()
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The whole §9b run
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The §9b comparative execution: every case, every tabulated entering
/// condition, every committed band row. This is the single source of the
/// recorded results file.
fn build_results() -> Value {
    let section9b_cases = load_section9b_cases();
    let section9_cases = load_section9_cases();
    let map = load_map();
    let fan_w = fan_heat_w();
    let ewbs = map_ewb_columns();

    let mut case_rows: Vec<Value> = Vec::new();
    let mut totals = BTreeMap::new();
    let mut engine_runs = 0_u64;
    let mut band_rows_total = 0_u64;
    let mut pass_rows = 0_u64;
    let mut known_fail_rows = 0_u64;
    let mut not_reproducible_rows = 0_u64;
    let mut missing_band_rows = 0_u64;
    let mut banded_cases = 0_u64;
    let mut no_band_cases = 0_u64;

    for case in &section9b_cases {
        let case_id = case["case_id"].as_str().expect("case_id").to_string();
        // The engine input is the §9a case definition (conditions, weather
        // binding); the §9b row supplies the bands and the notes.
        let engine_case = section9_cases
            .iter()
            .find(|c| c["case_id"].as_str() == Some(case_id.as_str()))
            .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!("§9b case {case_id} has no §9a case definition"));

        let runs: Vec<CaseRun> = ewbs
            .iter()
            .map(|ewb| run_case(engine_case, &map, *ewb, fan_w))
            .collect();
        engine_runs += runs.len() as u64;

        // The §9a case table names the licensed weather file the case is
        // bound to; it is quoted in the not-reproducible reason.
        let weather_file = engine_case["weather_file"].as_str().unwrap_or("(none)");
        let rows = band_rows(case, &runs, weather_file);
        let notes = missing_band_notes(case);
        band_rows_total += rows.len() as u64;
        missing_band_rows += notes.len() as u64;
        for row in &rows {
            match row["status"].as_str().unwrap_or("") {
                "pass" => pass_rows += 1,
                "known_fail" => known_fail_rows += 1,
                "not_reproducible" => not_reproducible_rows += 1,
                other => panic!("case {case_id}: unexpected band status {other}"),
            }
        }

        let runs_json: Vec<Value> = runs
            .iter()
            .map(|r| {
                json!({
                    "entering_wet_bulb_C": round6(r.entering_wet_bulb_c),
                    "outdoor_dry_bulb_C": round6(r.outdoor_dry_bulb_c),
                    "entering_dry_bulb_C": round6(r.entering_dry_bulb_c),
                    "total_capacity_w": round6(r.total_capacity_w),
                    "sensible_capacity_w": round6(r.sensible_capacity_w),
                    "compressor_power_w": round6(r.compressor_power_w),
                    "peak_cooling_power_kw": round6(r.peak_cooling_power_kw),
                    "required_load_w": round6(r.required_load_w),
                    "required_load_kw": round6(r.required_load_kw),
                    "plr": round6(r.plr),
                    "delivered_capacity_w": round6(r.delivered_capacity_w),
                    "delivered_power_w": round6(r.delivered_power_w),
                    "capacity_shortfall_w": round6(r.capacity_shortfall_w),
                    "shr": round6(r.shr),
                    "cop": round6(r.cop),
                })
            })
            .collect();

        let banded = !rows.is_empty();
        if banded {
            banded_cases += 1;
        } else {
            no_band_cases += 1;
        }

        case_rows.push(json!({
            "case_id": case_id,
            "case_name": case["case_name"].clone(),
            "series": case["series"].clone(),
            "banded": banded,
            "conditions": engine_case["conditions"].clone(),
            "weather_file": engine_case["weather_file"].clone(),
            "entering_wet_bulb_sweep_C": ewbs.iter().map(|e| round6(*e)).collect::<Vec<f64>>(),
            "runs": runs_json,
            "bands": rows,
            "missing_band_notes": notes,
            "comparative_note": case["comparative_note"].clone(),
            "comparative_series_status": case["comparative_series_status"].clone(),
            "status": if banded { "scored" } else { "no_band" },
        }));
    }

    totals.insert("cases".to_string(), json!(case_rows.len()));
    totals.insert("engine_runs".to_string(), json!(engine_runs));
    totals.insert("band_rows".to_string(), json!(band_rows_total));
    totals.insert("pass_rows".to_string(), json!(pass_rows));
    totals.insert("known_fail_rows".to_string(), json!(known_fail_rows));
    totals.insert(
        "not_reproducible_rows".to_string(),
        json!(not_reproducible_rows),
    );
    totals.insert("missing_band_rows".to_string(), json!(missing_band_rows));
    totals.insert("banded_cases".to_string(), json!(banded_cases));
    totals.insert("no_band_cases".to_string(), json!(no_band_cases));

    json!({
        "_doc": "Recorded ASHRAE 140-2023 Section 9b comparative execution results and per-case \
                 evidence-range rows (Issue #4666). GENERATED by the §9b harness \
                 (tests/validation/hvac_equipment_rated_performance/section9b_engine_run.rs) — \
                 re-record with FLUXION_SECTION9B_WRITE_RESULTS; never hand-edit.",
        "_case_table": "data/reference/ashrae140/section9b_ce_comparative_cases.json \
                        (generated by scripts/generate_section9b_cases.py, Issue #4273)",
        "_engine_case_table": "data/reference/ashrae140/section9_ce_cases.json \
                               (generated by scripts/generate_section9_ce_cases.py, Issue #4296)",
        "_performance_map": "data/reference/ashrae140/section9_ce100_performance_map.json \
                             (Tables 9-5..9-10 of 140-2023)",
        "_band_kind": BAND_KIND,
        "_band_policy": "Bands are read verbatim from the §9b comparative case table: every band \
                        is a Task-22 qualified-program ensemble evidence range, labelled '\
                        comparative evidence range, not a pass/fail criterion'. No band is fitted \
                        to the engine output, widened, interpolated between cases, or replaced \
                        by a flat percentage.",
        "_no_pass_fail_criterion": "Standard 140 defines no pass/fail criterion for the Task-22 \
                                    comparative ranges. The 'pass'/'known_fail' status of a row \
                                    means inside/outside the evidence range, never a verdict \
                                    against the standard.",
        "_comparative_series_status": "The ASHRAE 140-2023 Section 9.3 comparative test series is \
                                       not implemented in this tree and is not implemented here: \
                                       the CE cases are executed through the engine's §9 \
                                       equipment dispatch and scored against the committed \
                                       evidence ranges only.",
        "_entering_condition_policy": "The per-case entering wet-bulb is not transcribed for 13 \
                                       of the 14 CE cases (the 140-2023 §9 input specification is \
                                       licensed, #4285). The harness dispatches every case at \
                                       every entering wet-bulb column the map tabulates and \
                                       reports the envelope; it does not attribute a column to a \
                                       case.",
        "_metric_mapping": {
            "peak_cooling": "scored against the engine's full-load cooling power at the case \
                             condition (compressor power + 230 W indoor fan, adjusted-net \
                             basis). The ensemble semantics (peak cooling load vs peak cooling \
                             power) are unverified (bounds CSV source_page = pending).",
            "annual_cooling": "not reproducible: needs the normative TMY2 weather file (licensed, \
                               never committed); a steady-state dispatch has no duty cycle.",
            "max_zone_temp": "not reproducible: needs the annual zone-temperature trajectory; the \
                              steady-state dispatch holds the case setpoint."
        },
        "_status_legend": {
            "pass": "the engine value falls inside the comparative evidence range",
            "known_fail": "the engine value falls outside the comparative evidence range — \
                           recorded with the real numbers, never omitted",
            "not_reproducible": "the band metric cannot be produced by this run (coverage gap)",
            "no_band": "no comparative band exists for that metric/case; the §9b table's explicit \
                        missing-band note is carried verbatim"
        },
        "totals": Value::Object(totals.into_iter().collect()),
        "cases": case_rows,
    })
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Live-vs-recorded comparison
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Recursive comparison of two JSON documents; numbers are compared with a
/// tolerance (the recorded file rounds to 1e-6), everything else exactly.
fn json_diff(live: &Value, recorded: &Value, path: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    let mut diffs = Vec::new();
    match (live, recorded) {
        (Value::Number(a), Value::Number(b)) => {
            let (a, b) = (
                a.as_f64().unwrap_or(f64::NAN),
                b.as_f64().unwrap_or(f64::NAN),
            );
            let tol = RECORDED_ATOL + RECORDED_RTOL * a.abs().max(b.abs());
            let diff = (a - b).abs();
            if diff > tol || diff.is_nan() {
                diffs.push(format!("{path}: live {a} vs recorded {b}"));
            }
        }
        (Value::Object(a), Value::Object(b)) => {
            let mut keys: Vec<&String> = a.keys().chain(b.keys()).collect();
            keys.sort();
            keys.dedup();
            for key in keys {
                match (a.get(key), b.get(key)) {
                    (Some(x), Some(y)) => diffs.extend(json_diff(x, y, &format!("{path}.{key}"))),
                    (Some(_), None) => {
                        diffs.push(format!("{path}.{key}: missing in recorded file"))
                    }
                    (None, Some(_)) => diffs.push(format!("{path}.{key}: missing in live run")),
                    (None, None) => {}
                }
            }
        }
        (Value::Array(a), Value::Array(b)) => {
            if a.len() != b.len() {
                diffs.push(format!(
                    "{path}: live has {} entries, recorded has {}",
                    a.len(),
                    b.len()
                ));
            } else {
                for (i, (x, y)) in a.iter().zip(b.iter()).enumerate() {
                    diffs.extend(json_diff(x, y, &format!("{path}[{i}]")));
                }
            }
        }
        (x, y) => {
            if x != y {
                diffs.push(format!("{path}: live {x} vs recorded {y}"));
            }
        }
    }
    diffs
}

